<title>USA: General Electric unit wins $200 mln contract.</title>
<headline>General Electric unit wins $200 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>EVENDALE, Ohio 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>GE Engine Services Inc on Thursday said it was awarded a seven-year contract, valued at $200 million, to maintain engines powering American Airlines' Airbus A300 aircraft.</p>
<p>GE Engine Services is a subsidiary of General Electric Co, while American is owned by AMR CORP.</p>
<p>Under the agreement American will disassemble, reassemble and test the CF6-8OC2 engines, and GE will manage the repair and replacement of internal parts.</p>
</text>
